# Copy to vue/.env.production and adjust before running `npm run build`.
# These values are BAKED INTO the build at compile time by Vite.

# Base URL the browser uses for REST API calls (protocol + host + port).
# LAN example:      http://192.168.1.100:3000
# Domain via NPM:   https://api.example.com
VITE_SERVERURL=http://192.168.1.100:3000

# MQTT over WebSocket. Two modes:
#
# 1) Direct (LAN): leave VITE_MQTTURL unset and only set VITE_HOSTURL.
#    The app then connects to ws://<VITE_HOSTURL>:8083 (port 8083 must be
#    exposed on the server).
#
# 2) Through Nginx Proxy Manager (HTTPS page? REQUIRED to use wss://):
#    set VITE_MQTTURL to the full URL, e.g. wss://mqtt.example.com
#    (proxy host -> api:8083 with "Websockets Support" enabled).
#    Browsers block insecure ws:// from an https:// page (mixed content).
VITE_HOSTURL=192.168.1.100
# VITE_MQTTURL=wss://mqtt.example.com
